cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Live and Let Die: SAN MONIQUE — Special-Agent Mission Software"
abstract: >-
  PROJECT BOND film package (codename SAN MONIQUE). Deterministic
  special-agent mission software for the narcotics operation of Live and Let
  Die (1973): narcotics supply-graph analytics (max-flow/min-cut bottleneck
  analysis), budgeted network interdiction (greedy and exact solvers),
  voodoo-coded communiqué deciphering (keyword substitution ciphers, frequency
  analysis), Morse-timed drum-code signalling, farm-gate-to-street market
  economics, and Caribbean island ops planning over mangrove/crocodile
  terrain. Implements the BOND-API MissionProvider protocol.
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Daniel Ari
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6232-9096"
    affiliation: "Active Inference Institute"
keywords:
  - bond
  - narcotics-supply-graph
  - max-flow
  - min-cut
  - network-interdiction
  - substitution-cipher
  - frequency-analysis
  - drum-code-signalling
  - drug-price-economics
  - terrain-pathfinding
